# b21_variant_series_cap.test — issue #277: the per-variant result-series
# cap SKIPS the breaching variant and warns; it never fails the query.
#
# Every expectation below (case 8 excepted, see its own note) was CAPTURED
# from the pinned reference container and generated from its response
# bytes, never written from the expected rule:
#   image  docker.io/grafana/loki:3.7.4
#   digest sha256:87f0a067673756a3cede1bcbf0c74875f7df9b09fddb53e399d0c576f756cfcc
#   buildinfo version 3.7.4, revision b318f282
#   date   2026-08-12 (capture session)
#   config delta: `limits_config.enable_multi_variant_queries: true`
#   (`ci/logql/config.yaml`) — the bare container 400s EVERY variants query
#   with `multi variant queries are disabled for this instance`.
#   Anchoring: DSL `at 60s` was mapped to a wall clock instant on an exact
#   60 s boundary, so the container's /query_range grid points coincide
#   with the DSL's (the b15 anchoring rule).
#   Transcription discipline (PROVENANCE.md): the container's
#   `detected_level`/`detected_level_extracted` labels have no analogue in
#   PulsusDB's label model and are dropped from every expected label set;
#   values are unaffected.
#
# Dataset: one stream, 501 lines `id=<N>` 100 ms apart, N at offset
# (N+1)*100ms. Group counts are reached by filtering the COMMON range
# (`| logfmt | id < N`), because a bare variant's own selector and filters
# are dead syntax (`b13_variants.test` case 3).
#
# Shape: variant 0 is `sum by (id) (...)` — one series per surviving group,
# so it is the variant that walks the cap — and variant 1 is `sum(...)`,
# one series, so it is the variant that survives a skip. That pairing is
# what makes case 3 the per-variant-not-total proof: 500 + 1 = 501 RESULT
# series, served.
#
# PRE-COMMITTED EXCLUSION (a selection rule, not a post-hoc filter):
#   - case 8 (range at exactly 500) is a DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE. The
#     reference skips the variant there; PulsusDB serves it. Its captured
#     behaviour is recorded beside the case as a `# reference:` annotation
#     and MUST NOT be used to "correct" our verdict — see
#     docs/benchmarks/logs-differential-ledger.md entry (d) and
#     `range_variant_at_the_cap_is_served_where_the_reference_skips_it`.
#
# provenance: captured
# (file default; see logqltest/PROVENANCE.md §provenance markers.)

