# case 8 — range at EXACTLY 500 series in variant 0: PulsusDB SERVES
# it with no warning. THIS ROW IS A DELIBERATE DIVERGENCE, adjudicated
# on issue #277 and recorded as ledger entry (d).
#
# reference: the pinned container SKIPS variant 0 here and returns
# reference:   warnings = ['maximum of series (500) reached for variant (0)']
# reference:   surviving series = 1
# reference: because `multiVariantVectorsToSeries`
# reference: (pkg/logql/engine.go:474-508 @ v3.7.4 b318f282) tests
# reference: `len(sm[variantLabel]) >= maxSeries` BEFORE looking up
# reference: whether the incoming point's series already exists, so a
# reference: point belonging to an already-counted series deletes the
# reference: whole variant on the second grid point. Its own sibling
# reference: `vectorsToSeriesWithLimit` (:440-471) has exactly the
# reference: `!ok` guard this function is missing. Its INSTANT path
# reference: serves 500 (case 3), so the two disagree with each other.
# reference:
# reference: MEASURED REFINEMENT of the planned wording: the skip needs
# reference: at least TWO grid points. On a single-step grid
# reference: (`from 60s to 60s step 30s`) the same 500-series variant is
# reference: SERVED by the reference with no warning — which is what the
# reference: missing `!ok` guard predicts, since the delete can only
# reference: fire on a revisit.
#
# The values below are the reference's own bytes for the same two
# sub-queries run WITHOUT the variants wrapper, relabelled with the
# `__variant__` index the wrapper injects; only the skip DECISION is
# ours. DO NOT 'correct' this case toward the reference —
# `range_variant_at_the_cap_is_served_where_the_reference_skips_it`
# defends it.
eval range from 60s to 120s step 30s variants(sum by (id) (count_over_time({service_name="v277"} | logfmt | id < 500 [1m])), sum(count_over_time({service_name="v277"} | logfmt | id < 500 [1m]))) of ({service_name="v277"} | logfmt | id < 500 [1m])
